Onboarding steps (day-1 for a new bank)

1) PKI + Gateway
	1.	Issue client cert for the bank (or sign their CSR).
	2.	Add your CA to API Gateway mTLS truststore (S3 PEM).
	3.	Create API Key (bankX-prod) + Usage Plan; require on routes.
	4.	Keep Gateway JWT Authorizer enabled (we’ll feed it a Keycloak token).

2) Keycloak (internal only)
	1.	Create client: bankX-api-client (OIDC, confidential; service accounts ON).
	2.	Assign roles/scopes (bridge:deposit, etc.).
	3.	Add mappers:
	•	aud = my-enterprise-api
	•	org_id = bankX
	•	include roles in token
	4.	Copy client_secret. Do NOT share with bank.

3) RBAC DB (tenant & allowlists)
	•	Map cert subject ⇄ org_id=bankX
	•	Map API key id ⇄ org_id=bankX
	•	Seed allowlists (wallets, contracts, function_sigs).

4) RBAC exposes a /token endpoint (Token Broker)
	•	Bank does not talk to Keycloak.
	•	Bank calls RBAC /token over Gateway with mTLS + API key.
	•	RBAC authenticates bank (mTLS+API key), finds org_id, looks up bank’s Keycloak client creds, calls Keycloak token endpoint (client_credentials), returns the access_token (JWT) to the bank.
5) Bank calls your real APIs
Gateway validates:
	•	mTLS client cert ✅
	•	x-api-key usage plan ✅
	•	JWT (issuer/audience/signature) via JWKS ✅

RBAC Middleware (on the API path) then:
	•	Parses JWT → org_id, roles/scopes
	•	Enforces allowlists (wallet/contract/function)
	•	Proceeds with business flow

Bank → Gateway (/token): mTLS + API key
	2.	Gateway → RBAC (/token): pass through
	3.	RBAC → Keycloak: client_credentials with bankX-api-client
	4.	Keycloak → RBAC: returns JWT (aud=my-enterprise-api, org=bankX)
	5.	RBAC → Bank: returns JWT
	6.	Bank → Gateway (/bridge/deposit): mTLS + API key + Bearer JWT
	7.	Gateway: validates JWT (JWKS) + API key; forwards
	8.	RBAC: enforces RBAC/allowlists; executes


Pattern A (preferred — what you’re already designing)
	•	Partner → RBAC: mTLS + API key (no Keycloak secret).
	•	RBAC → Keycloak: uses stored client_id/secret per bank (in Secrets Manager/Vault).
	•	RBAC /token returns Keycloak access_token (JWT) to the bank.
	•	Bank uses that JWT + mTLS + API key for API calls.

